---
/**
 * /adult-drivers-ed/texas/drivers-ed-over-25 — the optional buyer (MOFU).
 *
 * Rebuilt 2026-10-13 on the hook → answer → loop → funnel recipe (ADE-PAGE-RECIPE.md). Query family: "texas
 * drivers license over 25", "texas drivers license over 25 written test", "do you need drivers ed at 25 in
 * texas". The first screen is a decision, not a "no": the answer says the course is not required, then says the
 * one thing it still changes (CLAIM wording only) and how DPS itself puts it ("highly recommended",
 * tpst.dpsRecommendsOver25). The sections then take the reader through the rule, the choice, and what never
 * changes at any age (the ITAD video, the vision and driving tests, the queue).
 *
 * Facts: src/data/ade-eligibility.ts, src/lib/dps-stats.ts (the median wait). §84.40(j): never promise a license.
 */
import AdeGuide from '../../../components/ade/AdeGuide.astro';
import { law, itd, fees, tpst, CLAIM, CLAIM_25 } from '../../../data/ade-eligibility';
import { dpsStats as W } from '../../../lib/dps-stats';

const base = '/adult-drivers-ed/texas';

// The one-breath answer. Same sentence in the meta description and the lede.
const answer = `No. Drivers ed isn't required at ${law.ageCeiling} and over in Texas, though DPS calls it "highly recommended." Passing it ${CLAIM}.`;

const faqs = [
  { q: 'Do you need drivers ed at 25 in Texas?', a: 'No. DPS states there are no driver education requirements for ages 25 and older. §521.1601 only reaches people younger than 25, so once you are 25 the course is optional.' },
  { q: 'Do I have to take the written test if I am over 25?', a: `Yes, at the DPS office, unless you take an approved driver education course first: its exam ${CLAIM_25}. A valid license from another U.S. state is the other way around it, since DPS exempts that transfer from the knowledge and skills exams.` },
  { q: 'What do I still have to do at 25 or older?', a: `Everything else: the application, identity, lawful presence and Texas residency documents, the $${fees.newLicense18to84} fee, the vision test, the knowledge test, the driving skills test, and the ${itd.adultName} video before that skills test. Only the driver education requirement drops away.` },
  { q: 'Is the course still worth taking at 25 or older?', a: `It can be, if you would rather not take the sign and traffic law portions at the office. Under §521.167 it ${CLAIM}, and DPS calls it highly recommended for first-time applicants over 25. Whether that is worth six hours and the price depends on how comfortable you feel walking into a written test on Texas traffic law.` },
  { q: 'Do I still need the ITAD video at 25 or older?', a: `Yes. DPS lists ${itd.adultName} as required for drivers aged 18 through 24 who must take an adult driver education course, and for drivers 25 years or older. The video requirement does not have the same age cut-off as the course.` },
];

const next = [
  { href: `${base}/never-had-a-license`, title: 'Never had a license, and past 25', blurb: 'No upper age limit and no penalty for starting late. What the path looks like.' },
  { href: `${base}/texas-written-knowledge-test`, title: 'What the written knowledge test covers', blurb: 'The parts the statute requires, and which of them the course handles.' },
  { href: `${base}/impact-texas-adult-drivers`, title: 'The ITAD video and its 90-day limit', blurb: 'Required at every adult age, and the certificate can expire before your road test.' },
  { href: `${base}/cost`, title: 'What the course costs', blurb: 'One price with the exam and the certificate in it, and the DPS fee on top.' },
];
---

<AdeGuide
  title="Texas Driver License Over 25: No Drivers Ed Required, the Written Test Still Is | Road Ready Safety"
  description={answer}
  url={`${base}/drivers-ed-over-25`}
  eyebrow="Eligibility · 25 and older"
  h1="Texas driver license over 25: drivers ed isn't required, but the written test still is"
  lede={`${answer} Without it, you take those portions at the DPS office. Three things do not change at any age, and one of them, the ITAD video, is the step people miss.`}
  faqs={faqs}
  dateModified="2026-10-13"
  updated="October 13, 2026"
  band={{ eyebrow: 'Optional at 25 and over' }}
  next={next}
  sources={[
    { label: 'Tex. Transp. Code §521.1601, Driver Education Required; Exception', href: 'https://statutes.capitol.texas.gov/Docs/TN/htm/TN.521.htm' },
    { label: 'Tex. Transp. Code §521.167, Waiver of Certain Education and Examination Requirements', href: 'https://statutes.capitol.texas.gov/Docs/TN/htm/TN.521.htm' },
    { label: 'Texas DPS, Apply for a Texas Driver License', href: 'https://www.dps.texas.gov/section/driver-license/apply-texas-driver-license' },
    { label: 'Texas DPS, Third Party Skills Testing Program', href: 'https://www.dps.texas.gov/section/driver-license/third-party-skills-testing-program' },
    { label: 'Texas DPS, Impact Texas Drivers (ITD) Program', href: 'https://www.dps.texas.gov/section/driver-license/impact-texas-drivers-itd-program' },
  ]}
>
  <section class="flex flex-col gap-4">
    <h2 class="text-[22px] font-bold text-text leading-8" style="font-family:'Outfit',sans-serif;">Do you need drivers ed at 25 in Texas?</h2>
    <p class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]">
      No. §521.1601 prevents DPS from issuing a license to a person younger than {law.ageCeiling} without
      a driver education certificate. It says nothing about anyone older, and DPS puts the same point
      in a parenthesis on its application page: &ldquo;No driver education requirements for ages 25
      and older.&rdquo;
    </p>
    <p class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]">
      The test is your age when DPS issues the license, not when you start the process.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="flex flex-col gap-4">
    <h2 class="text-[22px] font-bold text-text leading-8" style="font-family:'Outfit',sans-serif;">What does the course still change if you take it at 25?</h2>
    <p class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]">
      One part of the exam. Under §521.167 the course {CLAIM}, so those portions are done before you
      reach the office. DPS says this on its own testing page:
    </p>
    <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-border pl-5 py-1 m-0">
      <p class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px] italic m-0">&ldquo;{tpst.dpsRecommendsOver25}&rdquo;</p>
      <cite class="text-sm text-text-muted not-italic">&mdash; Texas DPS, Third Party Skills Testing Program</cite>
    </blockquote>
    <p class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]">
      If you have never driven, or you learned abroad and Texas signage is unfamiliar, six hours of
      structured material and a practice examination is a reasonable trade for not sitting a written
      test cold.
    </p>
    <p class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]">
      If you are a confident driver who never got around to the license, you may not need it. You can
      take the written test at DPS instead, and we would rather you did than buy six hours you do not
      have to take.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="flex flex-col gap-4">
    <h2 class="text-[22px] font-bold text-text leading-8" style="font-family:'Outfit',sans-serif;">What still applies to you at 25 and older?</h2>
    <p class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]">
      Everything but the course requirement. The ITAD video, the vision test and the driving test
      apply at every adult age, and without the course the written test is yours to take at DPS.
    </p>
    <ul class="flex flex-col gap-3 pl-5 m-0 list-disc marker:text-text-subtle">
      <li class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]"><strong>The {itd.adultName} video.</strong> Still required before the driving skills test, at any adult age. This is the one people miss, and DPS will not test you without the certificate.{' '}<a class="underline hover:no-underline" href={`${base}/impact-texas-adult-drivers`}>The video and its 90-day limit</a>.</li>
      <li class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]"><strong>The written knowledge test.</strong> Without a driver education certificate, you take it at the DPS office.</li>
      <li class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]"><strong>The vision test and the driving skills test.</strong> Both in person, both unchanged.</li>
      <li class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]"><strong>The appointment queue.</strong> Median wait for a skills test was {W.driveTest.median} days when we read the DPS report on {W.capturedOn}.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]">
      The whole sequence, from documents to the card, is in{' '}<a class="underline hover:no-underline" href={`${base}/how-to-get-a-texas-license-as-an-adult`}>how to get a Texas driver license as an adult</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</AdeGuide>
